COSC 3P91 – Advanced Object-Oriented Programming
Laboratory 5: Collections, Files, Streams, and Serialization
Department of Computer Science
Brock University
Winter Term
Overview
This laboratory focuses on the transition from in-memory data management to persistent storage and advanced
data processing. While Laboratory 3 explored abstraction through interfaces and generics, Laboratory 4 requires
students to manage complex data sets using the Java Collections Framework and ensure data longevity through
File I/O and Object Serialization. Students will implement systems that utilize functional programming via
Lambda Expressions to process collections efficiently and persist object states across system restarts.
Learning Objectives
By completing this laboratory, students will be able to:
• Use Java Collections effectively to manage and organize data structures.
• Apply Lambda Expressions and Functional Interfaces (Predicate, Function, Consumer) to simplify implementation and filter data.
• Implement Character-Based and Byte-Based I/O for sequential and random access data persistence.
• Utilize Object Serialization to write and read the state of an object into a byte-stream.
• Demonstrate the use of the transient keyword to manage class data members during serialization.
Given Problem Description: The ”Persistent Student Management System”
You are tasked with upgrading a basic student record system into a robust, persistent management ecosystem.
• Data Management: Use a List (e.g., ArrayList) to store a roster of Student objects. The system
must support filtering based on academic performance using Predicate interfaces.
• Character Processing: The system must read raw student names from a text-based input.txt file
using Character Streams (Reader/Writer) to demonstrate sequential access.
• State Persistence: To avoid data loss, the system must support Object Serialization. You must ensure
that sensitive data, such as internal system IDs, are not persisted by using the appropriate keyword.
• Sorting and Operations: Use Lambda Expressions to define custom Comparator logic for sorting
students and perform bulk data operations using the java.util.function package.
